.TH TIGRIS\-EXPORT 8 "10 November 2026" "Tigris 4.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tigris\-export \- a Tigris report in another format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tigris\-export
.B \-f
.IR format
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR logdir ]
.RI [ report.jsonl ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tigris\-export
reads the JSON Lines report of a run of
.BR tigris (8)
and writes it as SARIF 2.1.0, for code-scanning dashboards, or as CSV,
for a spreadsheet. The checks know nothing of either format: both are
made from the JSON, so they say what the JSON says.
.LP
With no file, the most recent run in the log directory is taken.
.LP
SARIF: ALERT and FAIL are errors, WARN warnings, INFO notes. An ERROR
(a check that could not run) and a skipped check are not findings about
the host: they are the invocation's notifications, and a CONFIG record
its configuration's. An accepted finding
.RB ( tigris\-accept (8))
is a suppressed result, its reason the justification. A result's
location is the check that reported it, on the audited host, and each
carries a fingerprint of its level, id and message, so that a dashboard
does not fold the findings of one check into one alert. The rules carry
their descriptions from the finding metadata.
.LP
CSV: one row per finding record, ERROR and CONFIG records included,
with the host, run, time, level, id, category, check, message, detail,
the acceptance and the compliance controls. Fields are quoted after
RFC 4180; a field that opens with =, +, \-, @, a tab or a carriage
return gets a leading apostrophe, so that a spreadsheet does not run it
as a formula.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " format"
The format:
.B sarif
or
.BR csv .
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write to
.I file
instead of standard output. It is written only when the whole report
converted; a report that cannot be read leaves it as it was.
.TP
.BI \-l " logdir"
The log directory: by default
.I ./log
if it exists, else
.IR /var/log/tiger .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was converted.
.TP
.B 2
An error: no such report, a newer schema than this
.B tigris\-export
reads, an unknown format or option.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
tigris\-export \-f sarif > report.sarif   # the last run, for a dashboard
tigris\-export \-f csv \-o findings.csv old.jsonl
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tigris (8),
.BR tigris\-diff (8),
.BR tigris\-accept (8)
